Z||000006||Turbo88||11-21-2001||10:07 AM||||If you are going for a slaveage turbo, you want to find something as close to your engine's displacement and RPM range as possible. You also want to find one that spins freely and doesn't have any play in the shaft. If you are going to invest the time and money into a DIY project, I would suggest atleast rebuilding the turbo. If you are looking for a complete kit, I am in the process of making one, Design One systems has one, and I believe there are a couple others. You might also consider TRiAD's supercharger kit he is building or read up on 1fst2m6's juiced 2.8. I believe he is cutting down into the 12s with it. <P>If you DIY, you will need to create a crossover pipe that will plumb the exhaust from both cylinder banks into a single turbo's exhaust turbine housing. I've seen different kits come up with all manner of mounting and placement of the turbo so that's up to you and ou fabrication skills. <P>Good luck with it and let us know how it goes or if you have any other questions.||||reg||1
